-Cross-situational resolution: for every type of records and meanings, a form resolves to a meaning of a repertoire without repeats exactly when every record bearing on the form offers it and every other meaning is missing from some bearing record. For enacted scenes: from every situation whose transition record groups the two-word encoding and whose repertoire has no repeats, after every history of moves and namings, every finite encoded sequence is interpreted as the assembly of its atoms exactly when, for each word, the earlier records and the namings heard along the history, each offering what was accessible where the learner stood, separate its atom. The coordinated history (coordinated 37) is an instance; naming from one place (stationary 37) fails separation, and naming a site from where its atom is not accessible (mistimed 37) fails coverage. The specified spatial arrangement and supported movement/naming history produce the previous binding construction’s exact interpretation inputs; separate witnesses cover actual response and access, retention and timing failures.
+<a id="conditions--条件"></a>
+## Conditions
+
+- Natural-number two-dimensional positions, Manhattan distance and range two, three identified operation sites, movement law, naming convention and schedule are supplied.
+- The acquired grouping/binding architecture is reused; the successful history has 37 declared support units, including five consumed by movement.
+- For the general laws, meanings are compared decidedly and the repertoire has no repeats.
+
+<a id="does-not-show--未表明"></a>
+## Does not show
+
+- It does not show how the schedule of moves and namings is formed.
+- It does not explain complete attention, perceptual categories, understanding of intentions or their evolutionary origins.
+- The primary evidence compared constrains automatic transfer but identifies no unique mechanism or evolutionary history.
+- **Counterexample:** Matching positions and name counts can yield inverted bindings through timing; a clear view omitting the target can mislead; access without retention does not bind, and insufficient support prevents movement or response. [source](·)
+- **Counterexample:** With a repeated meaning, resolution is not separation (Repeated); one record omitting the target can leave a wrong unique candidate (Omitted). [source](·)
+
+**Standard boundaries:** No ethical premise is used. The core declarations use no Lean axiom; the periphery declarations cited use only Lean's standard axioms (propext, Quot.sound, Classical.choice), as their receipts report.
